  ,"help_faq_general_1_question": "What can I do with PDF Seva?"
  ,"help_faq_general_1_answer": "PDF Seva helps you manage PDFs and files on your device. You can merge, split, compress, reorder pages, convert images to PDF, convert PDF to images, and add/remove password protection."
  ,"help_faq_general_2_question": "Where are my generated PDFs saved?"
  ,"help_faq_general_2_answer": "The output is saved to the destination folder selected during the flow. You can also set a default save folder from Settings → Default save location."
  ,"help_faq_general_3_question": "How do I change the default save location?"
  ,"help_faq_general_3_answer": "Open Settings → Default save location, pick a folder, and confirm. New outputs will be saved there unless you choose a different folder during an action."
  
  ,"help_faq_features_1_question": "How do I merge multiple PDFs into one?"
  ,"help_faq_features_1_answer": "Tap Merge on the home tools grid, select at least 2 PDFs, then continue to merge. You can reorder files before merging if the merge screen provides the option."
  ,"help_faq_features_2_question": "How do I convert images to a single PDF?"
  ,"help_faq_features_2_answer": "Tap Images to PDF, select 2+ images, then continue. Arrange images if prompted, and save the generated PDF."
  ,"help_faq_features_3_question": "How do I split a PDF into pages/files?"
  ,"help_faq_features_3_answer": "Tap Split, select a single PDF, then choose the page range or split options on the Split screen and save the result."
  ,"help_faq_features_4_question": "How do I reorder pages in a PDF?"
  ,"help_faq_features_4_answer": "Tap Reorder, select a single PDF, then drag pages to rearrange them. Save to export the new PDF with the updated order."
  ,"help_faq_features_5_question": "How does PDF compression work?"
  ,"help_faq_features_5_answer": "Tap Compress, select a PDF, then choose a compression level (if available). Higher compression usually reduces file size but may reduce quality."
  ,"help_faq_features_6_question": "How do I add a password to a PDF?"
  ,"help_faq_features_6_answer": "Tap Protect, pick a PDF (must be unprotected), enter the password, and save. Keep the password safe—without it the file can't be opened."
  ,"help_faq_features_7_question": "How do I remove a password from a PDF?"
  ,"help_faq_features_7_answer": "Tap Unlock/Remove Password, choose a protected PDF, enter the correct password when asked, then save the unlocked copy."
  
  ,"help_faq_files_1_question": "Which files are supported?"
  ,"help_faq_files_1_answer": "The app focuses on PDFs and common image formats. The viewer supports PDFs and images (including GIF previews). If a file can't be opened, check that the extension matches a supported type."
  ,"help_faq_files_2_question": "How do I find a file quickly?"
  ,"help_faq_files_2_answer": "Use the search feature in the file explorer screens (Files/Search). You can also open Recent Files from the home screen to quickly re-open recent documents."
  
  ,"help_faq_troubleshooting_1_question": "I can't see my files or folders. What should I do?"
  ,"help_faq_troubleshooting_1_answer": "This is usually a permission issue. On Android, allow storage/files access when prompted (or from system Settings → Apps → PDF Seva → Permissions). On Android 11+, 'All files access' may be required for broad browsing."
  ,"help_faq_troubleshooting_2_question": "Why did my action fail or produce an empty output?"
  ,"help_faq_troubleshooting_2_answer": "Common causes are selecting the wrong file type (e.g., protected PDF for actions that require unprotected), selecting too few files, or missing storage permissions. Re-try the action and ensure the selection rules shown on the picker are satisfied."
